{"content":[{"c":["PHICHOL*, PHICOL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Commander of Abimelech’s army, mentioned in connection with his ruler’s treaty negotiations with Abraham and Isaac (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.21.22,32","r":"Gen.21.22,32","rawR":"Gen.21.22,32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.21.22,32","value":"Gen.21.22,32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 21:22, 32"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.26.26","r":"Gen.26.26","rawR":"Gen.26.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.26.26","value":"Gen.26.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:26"},"). The presence of an army commander should have indicated Abraham’s vulnerability, but the adversaries acknowledged the superior power of Abraham’s God and thus sought peaceful coexistence with him."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"PhicholPhicol","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 21:22, 32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.21.22,32","rawQueryValue":"Gen.21.22,32","sourceRefExact":"Gen.21.22,32"},{"anchorText":"26:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.26.26","rawQueryValue":"Gen.26.26","sourceRefExact":"Gen.26.26"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"03acd76d9fcb3dff0e09298efda81eae8ed5750f7d11582c5232384ebc682a22","sourceItemName":"PhicholPhicol","sourceItemOrder":161,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PhicholPhicol","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Phichol*, Phicol","title":"Phichol*, Phicol","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}